  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical connections",
   "page": 20,
   "description": "The sensor on a two-wire host bus. SCL, SDA and ALERT each get a 5 kΩ pull-up to the supply rail and run to the host controller; a 0.01 µF capacitor bypasses V+ to ground; ADD0 is grounded, which sets the address to 1001000.",
   "parts": [
    {
     "ref": "U1",
     "type": "ic",
     "value": "TMP102"
    },
