    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    "The pull-ups may be larger or smaller than 5 kΩ provided no pin sinks more than 3 mA.",
    "SCL and SDA may be pulled up to a rail equal to or above V+.",
    "ADD0 tied to V+, SDA or SCL instead gives the other three addresses."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "supply-filter",
   "title": "Supply RC filter for noise reduction",
   "page": 21,
   "description": "V+ is fed from the supply through a series resistor of 5 kΩ or less with a capacitor of 10 nF or more from V+ to ground, so the sensor's own supply noise is kept off the rail it shares. GND and ADD0 are grounded; SCL, SDA and ALERT go to the bus.",
   "parts": [
    {
     "ref": "U1",
